# ---- derived / regenerable working data (see RESTORATION.md §6) -------------
# Decoded sources (245 MB), per-song stems (968 MB), separation inputs,
# ONNX model download, transient plots and logs are all reproducible with
# work/run_separation.py + work/run_all_restore.sh, and would blow up the repo,
# so they are not tracked.
work/src/
work/prep/
work/stems/
# the ONNX separator weights (174 MB) are downloadable, but the trained
# top-octave networks are 80 KB each and are part of the deliverable
work/models/htdemucs.onnx
work/logs/
work/plots/
work/__pycache__/
work/*.log
work/report.json

# ---- audio deliverables ----------------------------------------------------
# The 24-bit masters are enormous; the deliverables that belong in the repo are
# the FLAC masters, the 320 kb/s MP3s and the 16-bit WAVs.
restored/*.wav
masters/*.wav

# ---- misc ------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
